{"kind":"FETCH","data":{"headers":{},"body":"{\"questions\":[{\"id\":\"f8aa5258-0c34-407c-a909-cc8cd4227229\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Original Report-Style Passage 1: Urban Heat Planning\\n\\nA city review of summer preparedness found that heat risk was not evenly distributed. Neighbourhoods with little shade and large paved areas stayed warmer for longer, while outdoor workers faced repeated exposure during peak afternoon hours. The review recommended cool-roof programmes, shaded bus stops, drinking-water points and work schedules that avoid the hottest period. It also warned that planting trees alone would not provide immediate relief because young trees take time to create shade. The report therefore favoured a mix of short-term protection and long-term design.\\n\\nQuestion: Which is a short-term protective measure mentioned?\",\"hi\":\"Original Report-Style Passage 1: Urban Heat Planning\\n\\nA city review of summer preparedness found that heat risk was not evenly distributed. Neighbourhoods with little shade and large paved areas stayed warmer for longer, while outdoor workers faced repeated exposure during peak afternoon hours. The review recommended cool-roof programmes, shaded bus stops, drinking-water points and work schedules that avoid the hottest period. It also warned that planting trees alone would not provide immediate relief because young trees take time to create shade. The report therefore favoured a mix of short-term protection and long-term design.\\n\\nQuestion: Which is a short-term protective measure mentioned?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Providing shaded bus stops\",\"hi\":\"Providing shaded bus stops\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Waiting for young trees to mature\",\"hi\":\"Waiting for young trees to mature\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Replacing all roads with forests immediately\",\"hi\":\"Replacing all roads with forests immediately\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Ending every form of outdoor work permanently\",\"hi\":\"Ending every form of outdoor work permanently\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: SSC CGL English — Current-Affairs Passages Based on a Report or Editorial\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"dd0de231-99c8-4af2-b7ec-8ddcce466f37\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Original Editorial-Style Passage 4: The Right to Repair\\n\\nWhen a small component fails, consumers are often told to replace an entire device. This may be convenient for manufacturers, but it increases costs and material waste. A stronger repair ecosystem would provide spare parts, diagnostic information and products designed to be opened without damage. Safety and intellectual property concerns are real, yet they should be addressed through proportionate rules rather than used to block every repair. The goal is not to force people to repair indefinitely; it is to make repair a practical option when it is safe and economical.\\n\\nQuestion: How does the author treat safety concerns?\",\"hi\":\"Original Editorial-Style Passage 4: The Right to Repair\\n\\nWhen a small component fails, consumers are often told to replace an entire device. This may be convenient for manufacturers, but it increases costs and material waste. A stronger repair ecosystem would provide spare parts, diagnostic information and products designed to be opened without damage. Safety and intellectual property concerns are real, yet they should be addressed through proportionate rules rather than used to block every repair. The goal is not to force people to repair indefinitely; it is to make repair a practical option when it is safe and economical.\\n\\nQuestion: How does the author treat safety concerns?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"They are imaginary and can be ignored.\",\"hi\":\"They are imaginary and can be ignored.\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"They justify blocking every repair.\",\"hi\":\"They justify blocking every repair.\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"They are genuine but should be handled through proportionate rules.\",\"hi\":\"They are genuine but should be handled through proportionate rules.\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"They matter only for old devices.\",\"hi\":\"They matter only for old devices.\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: SSC CGL English — Current-Affairs Passages Based on a Report or Editorial\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"d1d28c28-9c6f-439f-9fbb-b4844389e81e\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Original Report-Style Passage 3: Inclusive Digital Services\\n\\nAn assessment of online public services found that digitisation reduced travel for many users but created new barriers for others. Some applicants lacked reliable internet access; others could open a form but struggled with unclear instructions or inaccessible verification steps. The assessment recommended simpler language, low-bandwidth pages, assisted service counters and a clear way to save partially completed forms. It measured success not by the number of services placed online, but by the share of users able to complete them without avoidable failure.\\n\\nQuestion: Why were assisted service counters recommended?\",\"hi\":\"Original Report-Style Passage 3: Inclusive Digital Services\\n\\nAn assessment of online public services found that digitisation reduced travel for many users but created new barriers for others. Some applicants lacked reliable internet access; others could open a form but struggled with unclear instructions or inaccessible verification steps. The assessment recommended simpler language, low-bandwidth pages, assisted service counters and a clear way to save partially completed forms. It measured success not by the number of services placed online, but by the share of users able to complete them without avoidable failure.\\n\\nQuestion: Why were assisted service counters recommended?\"}